3. No resale of the standard itself
You may not sell this work, in whole or in part, as a product — digitally or physically. This includes paid downloads, ebooks, printed books, paywalled access, or any offering where the thing being paid for is this standard or its content.

You may sell services, software, or training in which this work is used, as long as what you are selling is your own work, service, or tool — not the standard itself.

Examples of what's allowed:

Using the standard on commercial projects (paid client work, internal company projects, etc.)
Referencing, applying, or implementing the standard inside paid consulting or training engagements
Building and selling software or tools that implement, check compliance with, or are informed by the standard
Adapting the standard into internal company guidelines or checklists for your own use
Quoting or excerpting parts of the standard, with attribution, inside your own paid deliverables (reports, plugins, courses)

Examples of what's not allowed:

Selling a PDF, ebook, or printed copy of the standard itself
Republishing the standard (or a lightly reworded/repackaged version of it) behind a paywall
Selling a "compilation" or "collection" product whose main value is the standard's content

